FINAL ANSWER:
Top owner by surviving lines for each file type (`git blame -w -M -C`, HEAD, 18 files, 1,662 non-blank lines attributed, 1,995 with blank lines):

| Type | Top owner | Lines | Share | Runner-up | Bus factor (50%) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `.js` (7 files, 1,032 lines) | Troy Goode (2 addresses merged) | 564 | 54.7% | Douglas Christopher Wilson, 362 (35.1%) | 1 |
| `.yml` (6 files, 314 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 101 | 32.2% | Íñigo Marquínez Prado, 80 (25.5%) | 2 |
| `.md` (2 files, 253 lines) | Troy Goode | 71 | 28.1% | Jon Church, 59 (23.3%) | 2 (Troy Goode and Jon Church, 51.4%) |
| `.json` (1 file, 40 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 50.0% | Troy Goode, 12 (30.0%) | 1 |
| no extension (2 files, 23 lines) | Douglas Christopher Wilson | 21 | 91.3% | Troy Goode, 2 (8.7%) | 1 |

Bus factor is the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines together reach 50% of the lines counted. It is computed per file type here.

**Identity merges (guesses):**
- Troy Goode appears under two addresses: `<email redacted>` (605 lines, 93 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (44 lines, 2 commits). The `.js` figure counts them as one. This is a guess from names and addresses. The split per file type was not printed, so I can't give the unmerged `.js` figure.
- `<email redacted>` appears as both Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and alex94puchades. In `.js` that person holds 30 lines (2.9%) under the alex94puchades name, and the table did not merge them.
- I wrote nothing to `.mailmap`.

**Left out:**
- Reformat commit `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", Fiona Formatter, 2026-04-12) is ignored. It touches 291 lines in the plain count.
  - With it counted, Fiona Formatter would hold 291 lines (17.5%) overall, Douglas Christopher Wilson 376 (22.6%) and Troy Goode 554 (33.3%).
  - The overall bus factor would be 2 instead.
- dependabot[bot] is excluded: 10 lines and 11 commits, not credited.
- Copy detection is the default `-C`. The output named no person whose share moved by more than 2 points.

**Mechanical rewrites checked:**
- 136 commits holding surviving lines were examined, and 1 was set aside (`62628c0`).
- 5 more look mechanical and were kept in the counts:
  - `739dc11` "docs: reformat license" (Douglas Christopher Wilson, 17 lines)
  - `fcd2b56` "issue #42: (WIP) switch to ESLint; clean up" (Troy Goode, 11 lines)
  - `00d6eec` "build: use yaml eslint configuration" (Douglas Christopher Wilson, 9 lines)
  - `344ce1e` "build: <email redacted>" (Douglas Christopher Wilson, 1 line)
  - `9c2b59d` "build: <email redacted>" (Douglas Christopher Wilson, 1 line)
- I did not inspect these with `git show --stat` or re-run with `--ignore-rev`.

**Caveats:**
- The `.json`, no-extension and `.yml` groups are small, so one commit can change the owner.
- The `.json` result is exactly 50.0% for Douglas Christopher Wilson.
- Surviving lines say whose code is still there. They say nothing about quality, review work or deleted code.

